		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">49</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As there are 1000 elements in both the array, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of the array, so I will write all the elements of both the array in paper.
2. For finding the maximum in both the array, I have to start comparing consecutive elements in pairs. And update the maximum value</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">211.07099974715976</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3718.394645801928</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">348.4091545813991</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">150.15979817402092</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As there are 1000 elements in both the array, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of the array, so I will write all the elements of both the array in paper.
2. For finding the maximum in both the array, I have to start comparing consecutive elements in pairs. And update the maximum value</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">348.4091545813991</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">126.75</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">c</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">50</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.

We have 2 major phases in the implementation.
Phase 1: One is to read the elements of the both array.
Phase 2: Second is finding the maximum product

Phase 1
1. Read the length of the array 1
2. Read the length of the array 2
3. Read the elements of array 1
4. Read the elements of array 1
Phase 2
5. Now create a variable called max1 and initialize its value equal to absolute value of index 0 element of array 1
6. Now start from index 1 element of array and compare its absolute value with the max1
6.1 If max1 is greater or equal to that value then do nothing, otherwise
6.2 Update the value of max1 with absolute value of current index value.
7. Now repeat steps 6.1 and 6.2 for other values of array 1 till we reach end of the array.
8. Now create a variable called max2 and initialize its value equal to absolute value of index 0 element of array 2
9. Follow step 6, 6.1 and 6.2 for array 2 elements and max2 variable.
10. Now display the value of max1 * max2</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">26.25611733005792</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">4057.2104371202126</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">746.6917705246622</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">309.0707188634268</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following is what I came up with.

We have 2 major phases in the implementation.
Phase 1: One is to read the elements of the both array.
Phase 2: Second is finding the maximum product

Phase 1
1. Read the length of the array 1
2. Read the length of the array 2
3. Read the elements of array 1
4. Read the elements of array 1
Phase 2
5. Now create a variable called max1 and initialize its value equal to absolute value of index 0 element of array 1
6. Now start from index 1 element of array and compare its absolute value with the max1
6.1 If max1 is greater or equal to that value then do nothing, otherwise
6.2 Update the value of max1 with absolute value of current index value.
7. Now repeat steps 6.1 and 6.2 for other values of array 1 till we reach end of the array.
8. Now create a variable called max2 and initialize its value equal to absolute value of index 0 element of array 2
9. Follow step 6, 6.1 and 6.2 for array 2 elements and max2 variable.
10. Now display the value of max1 * max2</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
